1
00:00:00,090 --> 00:00:02,880
When a woman stops fighting with you,

2
00:00:02,930 --> 00:00:04,230
it doesn't necessarily mean

3
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:06,140
she's at peace.

4
00:00:06,190 --> 00:00:07,210
It might mean

5
00:00:07,260 --> 00:00:09,300
she's slowly giving up.

6
00:00:09,790 --> 00:00:11,990
Most men make the same mistake.

7
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:13,160
They think silence means

8
00:00:13,210 --> 00:00:15,220
everything is finally okay.

9
00:00:15,270 --> 00:00:16,340
No more arguments.

10
00:00:16,390 --> 00:00:17,660
No more complaints.

11
00:00:17,710 --> 00:00:19,635
No more difficult conversations.

12
00:00:19,780 --> 00:00:22,050
But here's what they don't understand:

13
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:23,790
a woman who keeps arguing

14
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:24,710
may still be trying

15
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:26,400
to save the relationship.

16
00:00:26,450 --> 00:00:28,120
Because behind every complaint,

17
00:00:28,170 --> 00:00:30,045
there's often a simple message:

18
00:00:30,510 --> 00:00:31,640
See me.

19
00:00:31,690 --> 00:00:32,780
Hear me.

20
00:00:32,830 --> 00:00:34,630
Make me feel like I matter.

21
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:37,470
At first, she asks gently.

22
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:39,180
Then she asks again.

23
00:00:39,230 --> 00:00:40,830
She tries to explain.

24
00:00:40,880 --> 00:00:42,860
Sometimes she cries.

25
00:00:42,910 --> 00:00:44,900
Sometimes she gets angry.

26
00:00:44,950 --> 00:00:46,860
Not because she enjoys fighting,

27
00:00:46,910 --> 00:00:47,820
but because she's hoping

28
00:00:47,870 --> 00:00:49,860
something will finally change.

29
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:51,180
And every time,

30
00:00:51,230 --> 00:00:53,080
she hears the same things:

31
00:00:53,130 --> 00:00:54,470
“You're overreacting.”

32
00:00:54,520 --> 00:00:54,990
“Not now.”

33
00:00:55,040 --> 00:00:56,940
“Let's talk about it later.”

34
00:00:57,260 --> 00:00:58,500
Until one day,

35
00:00:58,550 --> 00:01:00,600
something inside her changes.

36
00:01:00,650 --> 00:01:02,050
She stops expecting…

37
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:03,580
and starts adjusting.

38
00:01:03,750 --> 00:01:05,240
She learns to do things alone.

39
00:01:05,290 --> 00:01:06,870
To solve problems alone.

40
00:01:06,920 --> 00:01:07,720
To deal with things

41
00:01:07,770 --> 00:01:09,430
without asking for help.

42
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:10,890
She cries in the shower

43
00:01:10,940 --> 00:01:12,480
just so nobody hears her.

44
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:13,750
And slowly,

45
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:16,030
she stops telling him about her day.

46
00:01:16,080 --> 00:01:18,040
Not because nothing happens anymore,

47
00:01:18,090 --> 00:01:19,530
but because she stopped believing

48
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:20,905
you really listen.

49
00:01:21,260 --> 00:01:23,350
And that's the dangerous part.

50
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:25,360
On the outside, she looks calm.

51
00:01:25,410 --> 00:01:26,080
Quiet.

52
00:01:26,130 --> 00:01:27,500
Easy to be around.

53
00:01:27,550 --> 00:01:28,950
But don't confuse her silence

54
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:30,045
with happiness.

55
00:01:30,210 --> 00:01:33,100
Sometimes it's emotional exhaustion.

56
00:01:33,150 --> 00:01:35,220
Sometimes it's a goodbye,

57
00:01:35,270 --> 00:01:36,490
happening slowly,

58
00:01:36,540 --> 00:01:38,575
one silent day at a time.

59
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,070
By the time he finally notices…

60
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:42,570
she's already gone.

61
00:01:42,620 --> 00:01:44,610
Not necessarily with a suitcase…

62
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:45,745
with her heart.

63
00:01:46,050 --> 00:01:47,310
Then he says,

64
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:49,150
“She left out of nowhere.”

65
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:50,130
She didn't.

66
00:01:50,180 --> 00:01:51,510
She tried to tell him,

67
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:52,970
again and again.

68
00:01:53,020 --> 00:01:54,360
She was slowly walking away

69
00:01:54,410 --> 00:01:55,510
for years.

70
00:01:55,560 --> 00:01:56,980
He just never noticed.

71
00:01:57,330 --> 00:01:59,010
So if she's still complaining,

72
00:01:59,060 --> 00:02:00,860
don't immediately shut her down.

73
00:02:00,910 --> 00:02:02,330
Don't treat every conversation

74
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:03,560
like an attack.

75
00:02:03,610 --> 00:02:06,120
Sometimes she's not fighting against you.

76
00:02:06,170 --> 00:02:08,320
She's fighting for the relationship.

77
00:02:08,640 --> 00:02:10,540
Listen while she's still talking.

78
00:02:10,590 --> 00:02:13,260
Pay attention while she still wants to explain.

79
00:02:13,310 --> 00:02:15,730
Because sometimes the most heartbreaking moment

80
00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:16,910
in a relationship

81
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:18,890
isn't when someone starts shouting…

82
00:02:18,940 --> 00:02:20,915
it's when they finally stop.

83
00:02:21,450 --> 00:02:22,370
Send this to someone

84
00:02:22,420 --> 00:02:23,770
who needs to hear it.

85
00:02:23,820 --> 00:02:26,830
And follow for more.
